[{"id":117464,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/anti-ideal/near/117464\">#1</a> Currently “<a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/anti-ideal\">anti-ideal</a>” redirects to <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/antisubalgebra\">antisubalgebra</a>, which is less than helpful.</p>\n<p>I’d like to give it it’s own entry.</p>\n<p>But what’s a good canonical reference? Especially on anti-ideals in Lie algebras?</p>\n<p>I am asking because I ran into the following (simple) situation, which I’d like to address by its proper name:</p>\n<p>Given an <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L_\\infty</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">∞</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>-algebra <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"fraktur\">g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak{g}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6644em;vertical-align:-0.1891em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathfrak\">g</span></span></span></span> such that its CE-algebra <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"fraktur\">g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathrm{CE}(\\mathfrak{g})</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">CE</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathfrak\">g</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> has generators <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(e^i)_{i \\in I}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.0747em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">e</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8247em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\"><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3283em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span><span class=\"mrel mtight\">∈</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">I</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1774em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> and one more generator <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span></span></span></span> which is closed, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathrm{d} f = 0</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathrm\">d</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span></span></span></span>, then discarding that generator yields the CE-algebra of a sub-<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L_\\infty</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">∞</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>-algebra.</p>\n<p>This sub-algebra, I suppose, wants to be called the “quotient by the abelian anti-ideal” which is generated by the element dual to <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span></span></span></span>?</p>","timestamp":1727780315,"subject":"anti-ideal","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]},{"id":117472,"sender_id":17,"sender_full_name":"zskoda","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0ea9c6065e45ce1c059bd086dadd928e?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/anti-ideal/near/117472\">#2</a> <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span></span></span></span>Lab currently does not have a page named <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/antialgebra\">antialgebra</a> (nor <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/anti-algebra\">anti-algebra</a>). Did you mean <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/antisubalgebra\">antisubalgebra</a> ?</p>","timestamp":1727784064,"subject":"anti-ideal","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]},{"id":117473,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/anti-ideal/near/117473\">#3</a> Yes, sorry, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/antisubalgebra\">antisubalgebra</a>.</p>","timestamp":1727784616,"subject":"anti-ideal","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]},{"id":117477,"sender_id":1008,"sender_full_name":"Madeleine Birchfield","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f759fe50e1d01fe5f7869048a1e486cc?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/anti-ideal/near/117477\">#4</a> I don’t know about anti-ideals in Lie algebras but for anti-ideals in commutative rings there is </p>\n<ul>\n<li>A. S. Troelstra and D. van Dalen. Constructivism in mathematics. Vol. II, volume 123 of Studies in Logic and the Foundations of Mathematics. North-Holland Publishing Co., Amsterdam, 1988</li>\n</ul>","timestamp":1727803218,"subject":"anti-ideal","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]},{"id":117478,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/anti-ideal/near/117478\">#5</a> Thanks. I’ll make a little entry now</p>\n<p>(Let’s see if the software will post the announcement to this thread here or start a new one…)</p>","timestamp":1727806952,"subject":"anti-ideal","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]},{"id":117482,"sender_id":1008,"sender_full_name":"Madeleine Birchfield","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f759fe50e1d01fe5f7869048a1e486cc?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/anti-ideal/near/117482\">#6</a> The software will post the announcement on a new thread because this thread is located in the “Atrium &gt; Mathematics, Physics &amp; Philosophy” subforum while the announcements are posted in the “nLab &gt; Latest Changes” subforum.</p>","timestamp":1727808037,"subject":"anti-ideal","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]},{"id":117484,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/anti-ideal/near/117484\">#7</a> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/2/topic/anti-ideal/near/117483\">right</a></p>","timestamp":1727808249,"subject":"anti-ideal","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]}]